{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0CXY", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-not-flat}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a076e2d443539440da4039d80629104a94f30feb88a8ca3f98ef614e11ff92b8", "source_text": "The stack of coherent sheaves in the non-flat case", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3c9c7c06f4d9f3db039aa768b2f78c843104622be79a399d0a403f1ee47e8f84", "unit_id": "tag:0CXY:title"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CXY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-theorem-coherent-algebraic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{quot-section-not-flat}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2ff3ebdab5168793f574a562ef52da6b657b3806f6f5aa8049f62b18662740ef", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be94f6806599187f8a8906f2efceb762b3dc73a4f3d2c986a94371817b5bbaf5", "source_text": "In Quot, Theorem <REF_0001>\nthe assumption that <MATH_0001> is flat is not necessary.\nIn this section we modify the method of proof based on ideas from\nderived algebraic geometry to get around the flatness hypothesis.\nAn entirely different method is used in\nQuot, Section <REF_0002>\nto get exactly the same result; this is why the\nmethod from this section is obsolete.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8461f618fbdf01d978080f949b566a1692cc72270c53c1352922bd5499c63f21", "unit_id": "tag:0CXY:p001"}
{"chapter": "obsolete", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CXY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-theorem-coherent-algebraic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{quot-lemma-coherent-defo-thy}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{artin-section-dual}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{defos-lemma-flat-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{defos-lemma-verify-iv-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{defos-section-flat-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{defos-lemma-flat-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{defos-lemma-inf-ext-rel-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{defos-lemma-inf-map-rel-ringed-topoi}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\medskip\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f44d8976dc7ce625fd479abab0920a68e67896c3414ea482fae8af056c58e982", "source_text": "The only step in the proof of\nQuot, Theorem <REF_0001>\nwhich uses flatness is in the application of\nQuot, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThe lemma is used to construct an obstruction theory as in\nArtin's Axioms, Section <REF_0003>.\nThe proof of the lemma relies on\nDeformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0004> and\n<REF_0005> from\nDeformation Theory, Section <REF_0006>.\nThis is how the assumption that <MATH_0001> is flat comes about.\nBefore we go on, note that results (2) and (3) of\nDeformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0007>\ndo hold without the assumption that <MATH_0002> is flat as they rely\non Deformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0008>\nand <REF_0009>\nwhich do not have any flatness assumptions.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9aa5ae1ade2f106993dc002f714e529d263522cca325c64a01156f7c5cf70a76", "unit_id": "tag:0CXY:p002"}
